    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Allocator proxy.</para><para>Allocators are copied by value when containers are created, which means that each container would normally have its own allocator. However, sometimes, like for pool allocators, performance can be better if multiple containers could share an allocator. An allocator proxy allows containers to share allocators by having the proxy reference the allocator. When the proxy is copied, the new copy continues to point to the original allocator.</para><para>Example usage:</para><para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">Sawyer::PoolAllocator<sp/>pool;<sp/>//<sp/>one<sp/>pool<sp/>of<sp/>memory<sp/>for<sp/>all<sp/>graphs</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">typedef<sp/>Sawyer::ProxyAllocator&lt;Sawyer::PoolAllocator&gt;<sp/>PoolProxy;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">typedef<sp/>Sawyer::Container::Graph&lt;int,<sp/>int,<sp/>PoolProxy&gt;<sp/>Graph;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">Graph<sp/>g1(pool);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">Graph<sp/>g2(pool);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>    </detaileddescription>
